==encryption
encrypt file
gpg --output KWBDP.txt.gpg --encrypt --recipient MAIL KWBDP.txt
gpg -e -r KEYID|MAIL KWBDP.txt -o KWBDP.txt.gpg
also sign
gpg -s -e -r KEYID|MAIL -o KWBDP.txt.gpg KWBDP.txt
disable compression (large already compressed files)
gpg -s -e -z 0 -r KEYID|MAIL -o KWBDP.txt.gpg KWBDP.txt
stdin also works
cat "my secret message" | gpg -e -r KEYID > message.txt.gpg
encrypt using passphrase
gpg -c file.txt

